Give `add_resource` an optional resource-meta argument.

WHY: BundleManifestBuilder defaults a resource's 16-byte meta to zeros when
TryGetMeta fails, and ResourceFileReader always fails. For most resource types
that is harmless -- BF3's DxTextures ship all-zero meta -- but a MeshSet keeps
the length of its relocation table in meta field f2, so a mesh added through
`add_resource` today relocates nothing. `replace_resource` is not a substitute:
it inherits the ORIGINAL resource's meta, which is only correct while the new
payload keeps the same block sizes.

tools/usd/meshset.py already computes the correct 16 bytes; serialize() returns
them alongside the payload. With this patch:

    add_resource my/new/mesh MeshSet "/tmp/new.meshset" E0040000000000006000000070009400

STATUS: NOT COMPILED. The build was blocked by this environment's permission
classifier, so this patch is unverified -- it has never been through a compiler.
Review it as a proposal, not as a tested change. Apply from the Rime root with
`git apply`, and note that Rime is private: do not commit or push it.

